    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_7db1003f65110178d581ede0ad5e2a3fe6dbab7224736db4d4c278f94e2acd26",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Introducing ψ3 creates three explicit analytic obligations: its diagonal pairing I3 and its cross pairings I23 with ψ2 and I31 with ψ1. This interaction decomposition shows that the value of an added representation component cannot be assessed in isolation from the new pairwise terms it induces. From the visible zeta-factor counts, I3 is naturally interpreted as fourth-moment-like and the two cross terms as mixed third-moment-like, but that classification is an inference; the span itself only defines the unevaluated integrals and gives no asymptotics or admissibility hypotheses.",
